#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133877 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133693 :question/id #uuid "4e4236a9-d99f-50b1-803a-ab3aea5a673e" :question/math-academy-id "e-8743" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf{F} = y\\,\\mathbf{i} + x^2\\,\\mathbf{j} - 2z\\,\\mathbf{k}.$ Evaluate $\\textrm{curl}\\,\\mathbf{F}$ at the point  $\\left(-1,0,2\\right).$" :question/worked-solution "If $\\mathbf{F}=P\\,\\mathbf{i}+Q\\,\\mathbf{j}+R\\,\\mathbf{k}$ is a vector field on $\\mathbb{R}^3$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $\\mathbf F$ all exist, then the curl of $\\mathbf F$ is the vector field given by\n\n![](images/88/888b12c4f687dba1199a82d7e3a5e6897e7599ea812753423de5a23ffd756888.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{curl}\\,F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ y & {x}^{2} & -2z\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-2z)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2})]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-2z)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(y)]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)]k \\\\  & =(0-0)i-(0-0)j+(2x-1)k \\\\  & =(2x-1)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\textrm {curl}\\, \\mathbf{F}$ at the point $\\left(-1,0,2\\right),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\text{curl}\\,F)(-1,0,2) & =(2(-1)-1)\\,k=-3\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ad4e453-00da-5c77-8d6a-5de4dc3d5593" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048707 :topic/math-academy-id 1929 :topic/title "Introduction to Partial Derivatives"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049132 :topic/math-academy-id 245 :topic/title "Calculating the Cross Product Using Determinants"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134370 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d95192b-f90c-5222-9284-d5964b68929b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132260} {:answer/id #uuid "9811580a-9a4c-5cae-b93f-8fd017dafbe7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-yi - zj - xk" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132261} {:answer/id #uuid "09fbced1-93c8-576e-a89e-8374e5fcba7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "yi + zj + xk" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132262} {:answer/id #uuid "566a2e25-a40d-56a1-94ed-4593f8fbe01c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-yi + zj - xk" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132263} {:answer/id #uuid "7d7af965-ca09-5326-8611-2d1a13330464" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "yi - zj + xk" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132264}] :answer-field/id #uuid "f7886041-1fa1-565d-a7c5-c176ca25c68d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132259}] :question/id #uuid "c3a2ad27-232a-567b-825a-c40b631d791e" :question/math-academy-id "q-41883" :question/problem "Given that $F(x, y, z) = xyi + yzj + xzk$, what is $curlF$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134371 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83a235db-fe30-5523-a6f2-1e7015a51178" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i - πj + k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132266} {:answer/id #uuid "a24521cf-55f3-5015-939b-a0cc82725ed9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132267} {:answer/id #uuid "199823a5-e425-55bd-ac92-cb08df6ff59b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i - πj" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132268} {:answer/id #uuid "26bbb2ee-97a5-5ba6-a39c-bf211651dd8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- πj + k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132269} {:answer/id #uuid "6955754e-91e9-5e29-a742-fb32e4672dc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132270}] :answer-field/id #uuid "b6d59174-8d79-514e-8de5-8030757c35f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132265}] :question/id #uuid "edc90e26-2ff6-5c4d-97cc-a6c6e64cf17e" :question/math-academy-id "q-41899" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F = x\\cos yzi + y\\ln xzk$. Evaluate $∇ \\cdot F$ at the point $(1, \\frac{π}{2}, 1)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235539 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "badc07a3-1246-57ab-8020-ef66917b8e96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234832}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "badc07a3-1246-57ab-8020-ef66917b8e96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234832} :answer-field/id #uuid "c66b8368-5a95-5c46-b080-d106fa6765c0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235216} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1266fc86-1b5f-5a90-babf-82e935d1b03d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234568}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1266fc86-1b5f-5a90-babf-82e935d1b03d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234568} :answer-field/id #uuid "de4c731c-ed74-5645-8ab9-3c59ddda4a72" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235243} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0ef2d04-e954-5c3b-a12b-42687de0c911" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2z-{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234846}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0ef2d04-e954-5c3b-a12b-42687de0c911" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2z-{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234846} :answer-field/id #uuid "df422da9-b336-5913-a0b2-622e6c8e0a04" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235244}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a5631afa-3e26-5ef4-92ef-abe2aca2eb11" :question/math-academy-id "q-168621" :question/problem "$\\text{curl}\\,F\\,=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $⟨$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the curl of $F$ is the vector field given by\n\n$$\ncurl\\,F=∇\\times F=|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{curl}\\,F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ {z}^{2} & 2xy & x{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{y}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(2xy)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{y}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({z}^{2})]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2xy)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({z}^{2})]k \\\\  & =(2xy-0)\\,i-({y}^{2}-2z)\\,j+(2y-0)\\,k \\\\  & =2xy\\,i-({y}^{2}-2z)\\,j+2y\\,k \\\\  & =⟨2xy,\\,2z-{y}^{2},\\,2y⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241107 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1639f667-cc0c-541f-beb3-df7075bcd242" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6z\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238243} {:answer/id #uuid "746766cf-a9af-578f-8dc5-0e36b21b4e06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239054} {:answer/id #uuid "7681ef8d-3f67-572c-af5f-8f55918debf3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239078} {:answer/id #uuid "7de0f017-aa4f-55fa-b7f6-e4e3b289359f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6z\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239147} {:answer/id #uuid "e7823a5e-3336-5cc7-868c-2023128957eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6z\\,j+2\\,\\text{k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240093}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7de0f017-aa4f-55fa-b7f6-e4e3b289359f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6z\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239147} :answer-field/id #uuid "da2209b7-9fdc-539d-9358-25e617c5c773" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240714}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4b3b1abb-e804-5079-8fb6-32a843b8454e" :question/math-academy-id "q-105668" :question/problem "Given that $F(x,y,z)=3{z}^{2}\\,i+2y\\,j+k,$ what is $\\text{curl}\\,F?$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the curl of $F$ is the vector field given by\n\n$$\ncurl\\,F=∇\\times F=|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{curl}\\,F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ 3{z}^{2} & 2y & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(1)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(2y)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(1)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(3{z}^{2})]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{z}^{2})]k \\\\  & =(0-0)i-(0-6z)j+(0-0)k \\\\  & =6z\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241111 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "133c1b20-5150-50da-8523-674470a0cfe9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\,j+k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238215} {:answer/id #uuid "5c8be352-8015-5be2-b8df-9a4f3ad0aa93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238865} {:answer/id #uuid "82de7a70-0733-5cde-9eac-f208a1690d08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239194} {:answer/id #uuid "82fbfc1b-0c81-5da1-927a-375691efc6ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\,i+2\\,j-k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239197} {:answer/id #uuid "853fbdfa-bdb1-5373-adfe-5cf0720fa54b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i-2\\,j+k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239216}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82fbfc1b-0c81-5da1-927a-375691efc6ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\,i+2\\,j-k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239197} :answer-field/id #uuid "c42bc9e6-d9aa-54be-b2ee-e7d0d024b8b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240672}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b8f1a0a3-0b71-52cd-b327-6c0ec92e34be" :question/math-academy-id "q-105672" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F={e}^{y+z}\\,i+j+xyz\\,k.$ Evaluate $∇\\times F$ at the point  $(2,1,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the curl of $F$ is the vector field given by\n\n$$\ncurl\\,F=∇\\times F=|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{curl}\\,F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ {e}^{y+z} & 1 & xyz\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xyz)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(1)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xyz)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({e}^{y+z})]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(1)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{y+z})]k \\\\  & =(xz-0)i-(yz-{e}^{y+z})j+(0-{e}^{y+z})k \\\\  & =xz\\,i+({e}^{y+z}-yz)j-{e}^{y+z}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{curl}\\,F$ at the point $(2,1,-1),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\text{curl}\\,F)(2,1,-1) & =2(-1)\\,i+({e}^{1+(-1)}-1(-1))j-{e}^{1+(-1)}\\,k \\\\  & =-2\\,i+2\\,j-k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266075 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15bbc91c-fd98-5b6c-9665-d70f774533af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(z{e}^{yz}-y)\\,i+xy{e}^{yz}\\,j-xz{e}^{yz}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263203} {:answer/id #uuid "525a85d8-be7f-5e58-9de9-1e1199f1635c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-y\\,i+xy{e}^{yz}\\,j+xz{e}^{yz}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263710} {:answer/id #uuid "80f54f21-e7c4-5ec3-b1d5-b02fa7b3c8dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z{e}^{yz}\\,i+xy{e}^{yz}\\,j-xz{e}^{yz}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264109} {:answer/id #uuid "c704cdce-34fa-5e66-8fcd-a5d31c4900df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x{e}^{yz}-z)\\,i+x{e}^{yz}\\,j-xz{e}^{yz}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264741} {:answer/id #uuid "fd353914-244d-5acb-856d-77f4123cb4ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(z{e}^{yz}-y)\\,i+(xy{e}^{yz}-z)\\,j-{x}^{2}{e}^{yz}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265224}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15bbc91c-fd98-5b6c-9665-d70f774533af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(z{e}^{yz}-y)\\,i+xy{e}^{yz}\\,j-xz{e}^{yz}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263203} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcd0b969-143e-57e9-a012-fd5218ecced7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265575}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2c3cbbe9-4c45-5e2a-804f-38b6dd4503b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-131336" :question/problem "Given that $F(x,y,z)=x{e}^{yz}\\,i+yz\\,j+{e}^{yz}\\,k,$ what is $\\text{curl}\\,F?$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the curl of $F$ is the vector field given by\n\n$$\ncurl\\,F=∇\\times F=|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{curl}\\,F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ x{e}^{yz} & yz & {e}^{yz}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{yz})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(yz)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{yz})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x{e}^{yz})]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(yz)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{e}^{yz})]k \\\\  & =(z{e}^{yz}-y)\\,i-(0-xy{e}^{yz})\\,j+(0-xz{e}^{yz})\\,k \\\\  & =(z{e}^{yz}-y)\\,i+xy{e}^{yz}\\,j-xz{e}^{yz}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382847 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09e2916c-4330-5317-9940-8bd81420d877" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+2\\,j+3\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382849} {:answer/id #uuid "8313169e-da67-5084-89b9-6de60b1b433e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\,j+2\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382850} {:answer/id #uuid "add6679c-6145-570a-9b5b-d58274c5f26f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\,i-3\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382851} {:answer/id #uuid "64005279-cd6a-55f0-b1a4-4699a29fb345" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,i-j-k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382852} {:answer/id #uuid "d12556cf-9684-53a7-a211-1d901f057185" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "j-6\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382853}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64005279-cd6a-55f0-b1a4-4699a29fb345" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,i-j-k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382852} :answer-field/id #uuid "768eb6e6-1159-5455-954f-6daa92d3afde" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382848}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "27a8e275-9fb8-5aa1-b8f3-46200f4c3126" :question/math-academy-id "q-105698" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,i+y{z}^{2}\\,j+(x-z)\\,k.$ Evaluate $∇\\times F$ at the point  $(2,-1,3).$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the curl of $F$ is the vector field given by\n\n$$\ncurl\\,F=∇\\times F=|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{curl}\\,F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y) & y{z}^{2} & (x-z)\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x-z)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(y{z}^{2})]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x-z)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y))]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y{z}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y))]k \\\\  & =(0-2yz)i-(1-0)j+(0-\\frac{1}{x+y})k \\\\  & =-2yz\\,i-j-\\frac{1}{x+y}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{curl}\\,F$ at the point $(2,-1,3),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\text{curl}\\,F)(2,-1,3) & =-2(-1)(3)\\,i-j-\\frac{1}{2+(-1)}\\,k \\\\  & =6\\,i-j-k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383258 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62fd903f-e649-5428-9a2f-4c1aa5f6c22b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+2\\,j+3\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383260} {:answer/id #uuid "52796190-4740-539c-8e75-a6ad7f819b37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,j-2\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383261} {:answer/id #uuid "f7c8091c-bce1-56d7-80ae-658179937524" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-i+2\\,j-3\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383262} {:answer/id #uuid "8f933e4b-13c9-5280-a21e-056a60d49045" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3y\\,i+2x\\,j-z\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383263} {:answer/id #uuid "befb4236-3c4e-5e5d-85d6-2649a0ebfcac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383264}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "befb4236-3c4e-5e5d-85d6-2649a0ebfcac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383264} :answer-field/id #uuid "607af23d-3f74-5452-a712-45b9778ac8e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383259}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2c28fbe5-df41-51e5-b4b7-2d1414f882b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-131338" :question/problem "Given that $F(x,y,z)=x\\,i+2y\\,j+3z\\,k,$ what is $\\text{curl}\\,F?$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the curl of $F$ is the vector field given by\n\n$$\ncurl\\,F=∇\\times F=|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{curl}\\,F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ x & 2y & 3z\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3z)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(2y)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3z)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x)]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x)]k \\\\  & =(0-0)\\,i-(0-0)\\,j+(0-0)\\,k \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383265 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21985218-40b7-5d8e-a7c4-b8fb22c45c38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,i+\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383267} {:answer/id #uuid "f15f6c5b-022c-5634-b2a2-a72ef3b790e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,j-3\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383268} {:answer/id #uuid "81841eb6-fef1-55ac-961c-991a42be278b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\,i-2\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383269} {:answer/id #uuid "9fa83d83-20ef-5c72-8eb3-bcef1e295d9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,i+\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383270} {:answer/id #uuid "932f3e67-8dcb-55ab-a9a7-82af9923a07a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\,j+\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383271}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21985218-40b7-5d8e-a7c4-b8fb22c45c38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,i+\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383267} :answer-field/id #uuid "2056a6e2-aef3-52c4-ab48-744cca8dde53" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383266}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "119c787c-79ba-5ec1-aa8b-ef2fb283c3d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-131340" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F={x}^{2}\\,i+xz\\,j+{z}^{2}\\,k.$ Evaluate $∇\\times F$ at the point  $(-2,-3,1).$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the curl of $F$ is the vector field given by\n\n$$\ncurl\\,F=∇\\times F=|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{curl}\\,F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ {x}^{2} & xz & {z}^{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}({z}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xz)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}({z}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2})]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xz)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2})]k \\\\  & =(0-x)i-(0-0)j+(z-0)k \\\\  & =-x\\,i+z\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{curl}\\,F$ at the point $(-2,-3,1),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\text{curl}\\,F)(-2,-3,1) & =-(-2)\\,i+(1)\\,k \\\\  & =2\\,i+\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383272 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7851f0f-e955-50b1-bb5f-692cb729d280" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+j+3\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383274} {:answer/id #uuid "33eecef9-292f-5109-a112-0c1000c6dc0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+\\,j+6\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383275} {:answer/id #uuid "7edc97b5-9983-5cf8-b6da-26436232bb79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+3\\,j+2\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383276} {:answer/id #uuid "ba79d3eb-8cfe-5884-a1ff-8d90a2ca3b33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "j+6\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383277} {:answer/id #uuid "fc89b77e-7dfe-566f-87d4-07f18b28028f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+3\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383278}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33eecef9-292f-5109-a112-0c1000c6dc0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+\\,j+6\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383275} :answer-field/id #uuid "067c58e5-4d4b-51d3-bf82-b6a875039aed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383273}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c75d4d2c-54c4-5038-ab10-417305bd22e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-131341" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F=(2xy+2z)\\,i+({y}^{2}+1)\\,j+(x+y)\\,k.$ Evaluate $∇\\times F$ at the point  $(-3,0,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the curl of $F$ is the vector field given by\n\n$$\ncurl\\,F=∇\\times F=|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{curl}\\,F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ 2xy+2z & {y}^{2}+1 & x+y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x+y)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({y}^{2}+1)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+y)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(2xy+2z)]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}+1)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy+2z)]k \\\\  & =(1-0)i-(1-2)j+(0-2x)k \\\\  & =\\,i+j-2x\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{curl}\\,F$ at the point $(-3,0,-1),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\text{curl}\\,F)(-3,0,-1) & =i+\\,j-2(-3)\\,k \\\\  & =\\,i+\\,j+6\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385913 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f34066d-e5f3-59d1-b457-19e4e5363985" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385915} {:answer/id #uuid "6559cd7c-65d2-5d2c-b543-974d47b3bed8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e\\,i+2j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385916} {:answer/id #uuid "4e73f922-b725-5fdc-85a9-5d438d7e19cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i-2j+2e\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385917} {:answer/id #uuid "448ec01e-63d9-5985-be70-04517cbccf2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i-2e\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385918} {:answer/id #uuid "68728130-3e32-5eba-b606-02d0d2544d2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-i+e\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385919}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e73f922-b725-5fdc-85a9-5d438d7e19cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i-2j+2e\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385917} :answer-field/id #uuid "93fef15b-13ac-5973-a47f-908616ae5cb3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385914}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aeed6089-b923-5c58-9f18-b9dd1c803098" :question/math-academy-id "q-98894" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F=xy{e}^{z}\\,j+yz{e}^{x}\\,k.$ Evaluate $∇\\times F$ at the point $(0,2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3},$ and the first partial derivatives exist, then the curl of $F$ is the vector field on ${R}^{3}$ defined by\n\n$$\ncurl\\,F=∇\\times F=|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{curl}\\,F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ 0 & xy{e}^{z} & yz{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(yz{e}^{x})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy{e}^{z})]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(yz{e}^{x})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(0)]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy{e}^{z})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(0)]k \\\\  & =(z{e}^{x}-xy{e}^{z})i-(yz{e}^{x}-0)j+(y{e}^{z}-0)k \\\\  & =(z{e}^{x}-xy{e}^{z})\\,i-yz{e}^{x}\\,j+y{e}^{z}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{curl}\\,F$ at the point $(0,2,1),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\text{curl}\\,F)(0,2,1) & =(1\\cdot {e}^{0}-0\\cdot 2\\cdot {e}^{1})\\,i-2\\cdot 1\\cdot {e}^{0}\\,j+2\\cdot {e}^{1}\\,k \\\\  & =i-2j+2e\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Curl of a Vector Field"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133881 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133697 :question/id #uuid "cb99a3e1-9cd1-5335-b20c-01ad598d14bf" :question/math-academy-id "e-8929" :question/problem "![](images/71/71c58bf1b0fe4259ac50633a457f6a76639c0a0c188b66cce5e0fc3c7e5b0329.png)\n\n \n\nConsider the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $\\mathbf F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\textrm{curl}\\,\\mathbf F = \\mathbf 0$\n\n- $\\textrm{curl}\\, \\mathbf F \\neq \\mathbf 0$\n\n- $\\mathbf F$ is irrotational\n\n- $\\textrm{curl}\\, \\mathbf F$ points in the positive $z$-direction." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\textrm{curl}\\,\\mathbf F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $\\mathbf F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has curl at a point $P$, imagine that our vector field $\\mathbf F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\textrm{curl}\\,\\mathbf F \\neq  \\mathbf 0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\textrm{curl}\\,\\mathbf F =  \\mathbf 0.$\n\n![](images/86/86aee33cdfa96ac0a61468cc9657e791e399f31c024cdbc3a932193dc897d534.png)\n\nIf $\\textrm{curl}\\,\\mathbf F = \\mathbf 0$ everywhere in $\\mathbb R^3$, we say that $\\mathbf F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false, whereas statement II is true. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would rotate counterclockwise. Therefore, $\\textrm{curl}\\,\\mathbf F \\neq \\mathbf 0.$\n\n- Statements III is false. Since $\\textrm{curl}\\,\\mathbf F \\neq \\mathbf 0,$ the vector field $\\mathbf F$ is not irrotational.\n\n- Statement IV is true. Using our right hand, if we wrap our fingers in the direction of rotation (counterclockwise), our thumb will point upward. Therefore, $\\textrm{curl}\\,\\mathbf F$ points upward, in the direction of increasing $z.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and IV only.\""} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d42243ea-58fc-53f6-a0b6-f995bf1d697c" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048917 :topic/math-academy-id 3344 :topic/title "Visualizing Vector Fields"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134062 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64adfa84-016b-5b75-bfaa-1a8a86ec6cff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437398} {:answer/id #uuid "74db0023-87ca-59a4-a5bd-f3ec8e8116b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437399}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74db0023-87ca-59a4-a5bd-f3ec8e8116b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437399} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8d82e25-5382-533b-84b7-01e9f7a1d6d9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438728} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8567ee77-d4f1-5260-9f23-476c33065db6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437400} {:answer/id #uuid "a70669e9-818c-5056-9e48-6b53420d42e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437401}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8567ee77-d4f1-5260-9f23-476c33065db6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437400} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4ff09e7-c874-5a69-a376-7cc151c1b301" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438729} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bdbd1a0c-db83-58a6-82a4-5124aff61305" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437402} {:answer/id #uuid "66a86276-9dec-5106-ae18-146b9a8a0341" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437403}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66a86276-9dec-5106-ae18-146b9a8a0341" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437403} :answer-field/id #uuid "76eb44c2-5da3-5456-a3ae-c27f914fb121" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438730} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c36d028-9a19-523f-8a50-c043c1583d10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437404} {:answer/id #uuid "f9c4fd28-7364-51cd-9702-c77f2ad2fba7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c36d028-9a19-523f-8a50-c043c1583d10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437404} :answer-field/id #uuid "455d8cf9-d20d-599d-bbf0-180199060744" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438731}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7a72f589-a1bb-57d0-9bf2-23704868e98f" :question/math-academy-id "q-105092" :question/problem "![](images/38/38a7ae83a66a2c1ff6a012b9405c6621b0c0a162018065549e75a1d08bc04d44.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$\n- **II.** $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$\n- **III.** $F$ is irrotational\n- **IV.** $\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the negative $z$-direction." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has curl at a point $P$, imagine that our vector field $F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n![](images/59/594106633e422d24b9fea113d24fb6367fdef5ac52724931860e4163e33ce992.png)\n\nMoreover, if $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ everywhere in ${R}^{3}$, we say that $F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true, whereas statement II is false. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would not rotate. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- Statements III is true. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F=0,$ the vector field $F$ is irrotational.\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F=0,$ it points in neither the positive nor the negative $z$-direction.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134063 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba17fd4c-8a29-5e53-98c2-ac71e936d451" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439401} {:answer/id #uuid "829d51be-bbb4-5302-8892-638706b87aa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439402}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba17fd4c-8a29-5e53-98c2-ac71e936d451" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439401} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0a7c437-986c-533d-b681-b536d1087ea4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440058} {:answer-field/choices