/id #edb/ref 17592186440061}] :question/id #uuid "4556fe88-939e-5892-9221-116e661c0c0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-105103" :question/problem "![](images/04/04c6eb44298b639520994f01ef505ff40eba58307a1a40e7a48dfb0ebaae5d7e.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x, y, z)$, shown above. Given that $F(x, y, z)$ is independent of $z$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $curlF = 0$\n- **II.** $curlF \\ne 0$\n- **III.** $curlF$ points in the negative $z$-direction.\n- **IV.** $F$ is irrotational" :question/worked-solution "The vector field rotates clockwise with increasing magnitude away from the origin. Its curl is nonzero and points in the negative z-direction; it is not irrotational."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241106 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7dec2cc2-3405-52c3-8979-abd8eb2a2b24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437462} {:answer/id #uuid "0794f2ce-66e5-5eee-bc4d-0db5a27294c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437463}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0794f2ce-66e5-5eee-bc4d-0db5a27294c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437463} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b78da69-9857-55b5-bd09-bf9713a7e40e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438760} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66323cd6-6318-59a5-8c75-296ec59e3c19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437464} {:answer/id #uuid "421e51c5-959b-56e2-af2c-c59025f76191" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437465}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66323cd6-6318-59a5-8c75-296ec59e3c19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437464} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f5add59-bb91-5d45-ba13-41f76566398c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438761} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7c0fd7b-0c6b-5e56-bd17-a792412d0f1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437466} {:answer/id #uuid "78ef5d9e-ab86-5f26-8bdf-f69df52aee42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78ef5d9e-ab86-5f26-8bdf-f69df52aee42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437467} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff65ca0f-7924-5e1e-b45b-e82396f639fd" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438762} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c3454f9-4f94-5d9c-9504-95bd742d6fa6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437468} {:answer/id #uuid "a286c0c8-6b91-5628-897c-39200ea30c3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437469}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c3454f9-4f94-5d9c-9504-95bd742d6fa6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437468} :answer-field/id #uuid "daa53b8b-f892-5eaf-a4df-840413a09c4a" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438763}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d7d9f8f8-5aac-59da-a7d3-267484c84687" :question/math-academy-id "q-105667" :question/problem "![](images/77/773ff9d880deed92f8034d6949cfee85edbcdf735c8e125f1ec5762137fadb9c.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$\n- **II.** $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$\n- **III.** $F$ is irrotational\n- **IV.** $\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the negative $z$-direction." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has curl at a point $P$, imagine that our vector field $F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n![](images/4e/4e344a0a1f6b0c535c5ba08ee8c87914cf5e7009600f45732023720048b4c493.png)\n\nMoreover, if $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ everywhere in ${R}^{3}$, we say that $F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true, whereas statement II is false. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would not rotate. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- Statements III is true. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F=0,$ the vector field $F$ is irrotational.\n\n- Statements IV is false. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F=0,$ it points in neither the positive nor the negative $z$-direction.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241108 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87f8866c-3269-5305-94e0-80d60142b798" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437470} {:answer/id #uuid "ceaad2e3-2efd-5e19-bb7f-b57ea3fc6e7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437471}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87f8866c-3269-5305-94e0-80d60142b798" :answer/type {:db/iden