to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n![](images/59/594106633e422d24b9fea113d24fb6367fdef5ac52724931860e4163e33ce992.png)\n\nIf $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ everywhere in ${R}^{3}$, we say that $F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement II is true, whereas statement I is false. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would rotate. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statements III is true. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not irrotational.\n\n- Statement IV is false. Using our right hand, if we wrap our fingers in the direction of rotation (clockwise), our thumb will point into the screen. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F$ also points into from the screen, in the direction of decreasing $z.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266079 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77742b04-e958-51e3-885d-c186ce960ad8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437856} {:answer/id #uuid "7a46d360-0b63-59bd-8d4c-b0aa9e72d4a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437857}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77742b04-e958-51e3-885d-c186ce960ad8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437856} :answer-field/id #uuid "24781376-5a9f-5184-b064-24b3c476bb79" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438957} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d33cbee7-fc8b-5c3d-bfba-41b228bb82bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437858} {:answer/id #uuid "923