ect {:answer/id #uuid "20d194d4-bd3d-507f-8c59-044dbc7c81ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446555} :answer-field/id #uuid "9999ac46-6f4e-593f-907b-51eaf6bed9c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446569}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aedf76f0-5451-58bc-9366-057502daac94" :question/math-academy-id "q-126522" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=(3x+2y)\\,i+({y}^{2}-{x}^{2})\\,j.$ Evaluate the scalar curl of $F$ at the point $(-2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the *scalar* curl of $F$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}-{x}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3x+2y) \\\\  & =-2x-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the scalar curl at the point $(-2,1),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})}_{(-2,1)} & =-2(-2)-2 \\\\  & =4-2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Scalar Curl of a Vector Field"}]}
